Context('Numeric'); $v = random(45, 90, 1); $t = NumberWithUnits(($v+sqrt($v**2 + 384))/32, 'seconds');
############################# # Exercise Group Introduction #############################
BEGIN_PGML On Earth, if you throw a baseball straight up at speed [`v`] (in feet per second), it will land after [`\frac{v+\sqrt{v^2+384}}{32}`] seconds.
END_PGML
###### # Body ######
BEGIN_PGML If thrown straight up with speed [`[$v]`] feet per second, how long will it be until the baseball hits the ground?
[_]{$t}{10}
END_PGML
